    slReading: (): Part[] => ['On the sleep stage the gain is the hidden layer’s: the same layer not told the question scored ', srPp(s2s.estimate_pp), ' above the fixed heads (B-sh − B-lin, secondary S2; ', ...iv(s2s), '), and C1 − B-sh was ', srPp(p5[2].estimate_pp), ' (', ...iv(p5[2]), `), B-sh non-inferior at ${DELTA} pp; on frozen CBraMod features C1 − B-sh was equivalent within ±${DELTA} pp on all three questions. Sharing the trunk, against separate models, was inconclusive on the sleep stage. On frozen CBraMod features the fixed heads were equivalent within ±${DELTA} pp of the conditioned head on the sleep stage and the half of the night, not on the next change (`, srPp(p4s[1].estimate_pp), ', ', ...iv(p4s[1]), '). Five-stage accuracy on the small EEGNet trunk is modest: ', f(arm(B, 'E1', 'B-lin', 'SL-A').mean), ' with fixed heads and ', f(arm(B, 'E1', 'C1', 'SL-A').mean), ' with the conditioned head, against a chance of ', f(arm(B, 'E1', 'B-lin', 'SL-A').chance), '; fixed heads on frozen CBraMod features reach ', f(arm(B, 'L1', 'B-lin-fz-sgd', 'SL-A').mean), '.'],
    slArmsCaption: (): Part[] => ['Balanced accuracy of each set-up: the mean over ', n(B.people), ' people with its 95% interval. Chance is ', f(gate(B, 'E1', 'SL-A').chance), ' for the sleep stage and ', f(gate(B, 'E1', 'SL-E').chance), ' for the other two; the gate’s floors are ', f(gate(B, 'E1', 'SL-A').floor), ' and ', f(gate(B, 'E1', 'SL-E').floor), '. Overlapping intervals are not ranked.'],
